{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'One screen', title: 'Scattered weather data,<br>gathered in one grid',
  shots: [ { src: shots + '01_main_menu.webp', alt: 'App main menu — 12-channel grid for satellite, radar, typhoon, yellow dust, and CCTV', w: 720, h: 1533 } ] }) %}
  <p>On the Meteorological Agency site, satellite, radar, typhoon, yellow dust, temperature and local forecasts each live in separate menus. Weather Satellite Live gathers them into a single grid menu, and any channel you tap starts auto-playing from the latest image as a time-lapse.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>12 channels</strong> — satellite, radar, typhoon, yellow dust and CCTV on one screen</li>
    <li><strong>Auto-play from the latest frame</strong>, with pause and zoom at the bottom</li>
    <li>Every frame shows its <strong>observation time (KST)</strong></li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Satellite', title: 'Visible, infrared, water vapor:<br>three ways to see the sky', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '02_visible_korea.webp', alt: 'Visible Korea satellite — auto-playing time-lapse', w: 720, h: 1533 },
    { src: shots + '04_visible_earth.webp', alt: 'Visible Earth — full disc imagery down toward the equator', w: 720, h: 1533 }
  ] }) %}
  <p>Imagery from the GEO-KOMPSAT-2A satellite comes in nine channel × region combinations. Pick a tight view of cloud development near the peninsula, a wider East Asia flow, or pull all the way out to near-equator scale.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Visible</strong> shows cloud shape and thickness by day; <strong>infrared</strong> shows clouds even at night</li>
    <li><strong>Water vapor</strong> shows upper-level moisture flow — read heavy rain and typhoon buildup ahead of time</li>
    <li>Korea · East Asia · Earth, with <strong>pinch zoom and drag pan</strong> to focus on one area</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Radar', title: 'Where the rain is,<br>right now',
  shots: [ { src: shots + '06_radar_korea.webp', alt: 'Radar Korea — composite precipitation radar replayed as a time-lapse', w: 720, h: 1533 } ] }) %}
  <p>Composite precipitation radar from the Meteorological Agency, replayed in time order. Rainfall intensity is color-coded, so heavy-rain zones across the peninsula are visible at a glance.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Korea · Neighbors · Detail · Infrared composite</strong></li>
    <li><strong>9 local radar sites</strong> from Baengnyeongdo to Jeju for rain close to home</li>
    <li>Satellite IR blended with radar shows <strong>clouds and rainfall together</strong></li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Typhoon · Yellow dust', title: 'Read the track<br>before it arrives', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [ { src: shots + '10_typhoon.webp', alt: 'Typhoon — satellite infrared time-lapse to read the storm\'s track', w: 720, h: 1533 } ] }) %}
  <p>When a typhoon is active, the app plays a satellite infrared time-lapse so you can follow where it formed, where it's heading, and how fast it's closing in. In dust season, the same time-lapse shows incoming yellow-dust paths.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Satellite imagery shows the <strong>storm's eye and outer cloud bands</strong> as they look</li>
    <li>Observation timestamps let you gauge <strong>how far it has traveled</strong></li>
    <li>Yellow-dust imagery shows <strong>incoming fine-dust paths</strong></li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Road CCTV', title: 'After the sky, the road',
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '12_radar_cctv.webp', alt: 'Radar CCTV — precipitation radar and road camera markers on one map', w: 720, h: 1533 },
